    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner create.\n\n**What the spec needed:** on a successful `POST /api/owners`, emit a line via the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the `memberId`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New function class** `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` \u2014 a single-public-method OfficeFloor step that reads the persisted `Owner` from the pipeline variable (`@Val Owner`) and logs through the dedicated `NOTIFY` SLF4J logger:\n   ```\n   NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n   ```\n   It's modeled on the existing `AuditOwnerCreated`/`EmitOwnerCreatedEvent` audit steps, which use the same logger-per-checkpoint convention.\n\n2. **Wired into the pipeline** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `notifyWelcome` step between `emitEvent` and `record`, so it runs after `SaveOwner` (owner has an id) and `AssignMemberId` (member id is set), under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes (it captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts the line contains both the owner id and the fetched `memberId`), and the full suite builds green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
